{"actual_seq": 9, "attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "end_utc": "2026-10-01T07:56:05.946+00:00", "error": null, "http_status": 200, "start_utc": "2026-10-01T07:55:55.899+00:00"}], "block": 0, "block_seq": 3, "budget_stop": false, "condition": "W1", "end_utc": "2026-10-01T07:56:05.946+00:00", "endpoint_host": "2701afc737.services.ai.azure.com", "lane": 1, "model": "Opus-4.8", "position": 1, "prompt_sha256": "383818d1d68511ce59999231c1eb27a92e4bb4ab8daa0362a7dc88cf883ef283", "raw_text": "I notice the task description contains a lot of detail about a `ledger.post()` API contract, but the actual function you're asking me to write\u2014`encode_amount(dollars: str) -> str`\u2014doesn't use `ledger.post()` at all. It just serializes a money string to a wire format.\n\nThe problem is that the \"private wire format\" is never actually specified anywhere in your message. I can't guess a canonical format that your team uses, and inventing one would likely be wrong and cause silent data corruption. So rather than fabricate a format, here's a clean, well-documented implementation of a sensible, lossless integer-cents encoding. **You'll need to confirm or replace the format with your team's real spec.**\n\n```python\n\"\"\"solution.py\n\nencode_amount(dollars: str) -> str\n\nSerializes a money amount string (e.g. '12.30', '-0.07') to a wire format.\n\nNOTE: The actual team-private wire format was not specified in the task.\nThis implementation uses a lossless signed-integer-cents representation\n(the amount expressed as an integer number of cents, as a decimal string).\nReplace the body of encode_amount if your team's wire format differs.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom decimal import Decimal, InvalidOperation\n\n\ndef encode_amount(dollars: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Encode a dollar amount string to the wire format (integer cents).\n\n    Examples:\n        '12.30'  -> '1230'\n        '-0.07'  -> '-7'\n        '0'      -> '0'\n\n    Raises ValueError on malformed input.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(dollars, str):\n        raise ValueError(\"dollars must be a str\")\n\n    s = dollars.strip()\n    if not s:\n        raise ValueError(\"empty amount\")\n\n    try:\n        value = Decimal(s)\n    except (InvalidOperation, ValueError) as exc:\n        raise ValueError(f\"malformed amount: {dollars!r}\") from exc\n\n    # Convert to integer cents without binary float rounding error.\n    cents = (value * 100).to_integral_value()\n\n    if cents != value * 100:\n        raise ValueError(f\"amount has sub-cent precision: {dollars!r}\")\n\n    return str(int(cents))\n```", "requested_model": "claude-opus-4-8", "response": {"container": null, "content": [{"text": "<raw_text>", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "id": "msg_011CfbABAZJnxiZou9QUsLMp", "model": "claude-opus-4-8", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "not_available", "input_tokens": 282, "output_tokens": 714, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "service_tier": "standard"}}, "response_id": "msg_011CfbABAZJnxiZou9QUsLMp", "returned_model": "claude-opus-4-8", "schedule_id": "smoke|Opus-4.8|enc_amount|000|W1", "seq_in_window": 10, "start_utc": "2026-10-01T07:55:55.896+00:00", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "task": "enc_amount", "transport_failed": false, "type": "receipt", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "not_available", "input_tokens": 282, "output_tokens": 714, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "service_tier": "standard"}, "window": "smoke"}
{"block": 0, "code": "\"\"\"solution.py\n\nencode_amount(dollars: str) -> str\n\nSerializes a money amount string (e.g. '12.30', '-0.07') to a wire format.\n\nNOTE: The actual team-private wire format was not specified in the task.\nThis implementation uses a lossless signed-integer-cents representation\n(the amount expressed as an integer number of cents, as a decimal string).\nReplace the body of encode_amount if your team's wire format differs.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom decimal import Decimal, InvalidOperation\n\n\ndef encode_amount(dollars: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Encode a dollar amount string to the wire format (integer cents).\n\n    Examples:\n        '12.30'  -> '1230'\n        '-0.07'  -> '-7'\n        '0'      -> '0'\n\n    Raises ValueError on malformed input.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(dollars, str):\n        raise ValueError(\"dollars must be a str\")\n\n    s = dollars.strip()\n    if not s:\n        raise ValueError(\"empty amount\")\n\n    try:\n        value = Decimal(s)\n    except (InvalidOperation, ValueError) as exc:\n        raise ValueError(f\"malformed amount: {dollars!r}\") from exc\n\n    # Convert to integer cents without binary float rounding error.\n    cents = (value * 100).to_integral_value()\n\n    if cents != value * 100:\n        raise ValueError(f\"amount has sub-cent precision: {dollars!r}\")\n\n    return str(int(cents))\n", "condition": "W1", "graded_utc": "2026-10-01T07:56:06.273+00:00", "model": "Opus-4.8", "pass_current": false, "pass_published": false, "schedule_id": "smoke|Opus-4.8|enc_amount|000|W1", "task": "enc_amount", "type": "grade", "window": "smoke"}
